# Measured 2026-09-02 from testapp/output/screenshots/<pn>-ios-final-20260902-*.png
# Device: iPhone 16 simulator (IOS_SIM_DEVICE=swift-cross-ui) -- window 393 x 852 pt.
# Capture was 1179 x 2556 px, i.e. 3:1. Every coordinate below is px/3, in points,
# which is what the XCUITest runner normalises against window.frame.
# UNVERIFIED: coordinates were read off a capture of the running app; no row here
# has been replayed and seen to have the effect it predicts.
#
# P1: one tap only. The dialog it opens is a presented view controller and the
# iOS runner has no key it can send to dismiss one -- no Escape row exists here
# because XCUITest rows are taps and there is no measured coordinate for a
# sheet that did not exist when the capture was taken. The file therefore stops
# at the open and the evidence is the status line plus a screenshot.
#
# Re-aimed 2026-10-16 on the iPhone 17 simulator (402 x 874 pt). The open tap was
# inside the button already; the 2026-09-27 "misaimed" was the sweep's rule that a
# file is unconfirmed until replayed and seen. The picker's own X is now a measured
# coordinate (from p1-ios-final-20261016-025545.png, 3:1), so the file closes it, and
# the replay ended on "Open: Cancelled" (p1-ios-final-20261016-025749.png).
# 2026-10-16 於 iPhone 17 模擬器重新瞄準：開啟的點擊本來就落在按鈕內;現在加上關閉選擇器的 X,
# 重放結束時狀態列為「Open: Cancelled」。
click,310,166,client,left,,,"Open file dialog -- at the centre of Button 'Open file dialog' {{251,155},{119,22}} in the 2026-10-16 --dump-tree",ios
sleep,,,,,,2000000,let the picker animate in,ios
click,309,100,client,left,,,"the picker's X (close) -- the Open line must then read Open: Cancelled",ios
sleep,,,,,,1500000,let the picker dismiss and the status line redraw,ios
